---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AdsChecks Refund Policy | Completed Checks and Billing Errors"
  description="Read the AdsChecks refund policy for completed checks, duplicate purchases, billing disputes, and manual review cases."
  canonical="https://adschecks.com/refund-policy/"
  bodyClass="page-refund-policy"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "AdsChecks",
      "url": "https://adschecks.com",
      "email": "contact@adschecks.com",
      "description": "Ad slot verification with proof-first reporting."
    })}></script>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "item": { "@id": "https://adschecks.com/", "name": "AdsChecks" } },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "item": { "@id": "https://adschecks.com/refund-policy/", "name": "Refund Policy" } }
      ]
    })}></script>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal-page legal-page--wide">
      <div class="doc-hero">
        <div class="doc-hero__copy">
          <p class="section__eyebrow mono">Billing review</p>
          <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
          <p class="lead">Refund rules for verified page plans, delivered verification outcomes, and billing disputes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-hero__meta">
          <div class="doc-meta__item">
            <div class="doc-meta__k">Non-refundable unit</div>
            <div class="doc-meta__v">Completed verified pages, including CHALLENGE_DETECTED and BLOCKED.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-meta__item">
            <div class="doc-meta__k">Manual review</div>
            <div class="doc-meta__v">Duplicate or clearly accidental charges can be reviewed.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-meta__item">
            <div class="doc-meta__k">Contact</div>
            <div class="doc-meta__v"><a href="mailto:contact@adschecks.com">contact@adschecks.com</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-grid">
        <div class="doc-card doc-card--span-2">
          <h2>Merchant of Record</h2>
          <p>
            All purchases are processed by <strong>Paddle.com Market Limited</strong> as Merchant of Record.
            Refund requests can be submitted to Paddle via your account dashboard or at
            <a href="mailto:support@paddle.com">support@paddle.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            This policy defines AdsChecks' approach to refund eligibility. Final refund processing is handled
            by Paddle in accordance with their merchant policies and applicable consumer protection laws.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card doc-card--span-2">
          <h2>EU right of withdrawal</h2>
          <p>
            EU consumers have 14 days from purchase to cancel for any reason under Directive 2011/83/EU.
            If you explicitly request that verification services begin immediately during the withdrawal period,
            you acknowledge that:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>You waive the right to cancel once checks commence</li>
            <li>You are liable for completed verified pages on a pro-rata basis</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To exercise your withdrawal right, contact
            <a href="mailto:contact@adschecks.com">contact@adschecks.com</a> or Paddle support within 14 days of purchase.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card doc-card--summary doc-card--accent doc-card--span-2">
          <h2>General rule</h2>
          <p>
            AdsChecks is an evidence service. Verification outcomes and evidence artifacts form part of the delivered result.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card doc-card--span-2">
          <h2>Completed verified pages</h2>
          <p>
            Completed verified pages are not refundable, including results with statuses OK, SLOT_EMPTY,
            CHALLENGE_DETECTED, and BLOCKED.
          </p>
          <p>
            CHALLENGE_DETECTED and BLOCKED are valid verification outcomes, not platform errors. If the page load completed
            and the result package was produced, the job is treated as delivered.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Non-use and unused capacity</h2>
          <p>
            Unused monthly capacity, unused access time, or a decision not to run checks does not create a right to refund.
          </p>
          <p>Pre-purchase discussions, access review, or onboarding coordination do not create a refund entitlement.</p>
          <p>Billing starts only after a paid plan or other commercial terms are confirmed.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Duplicate purchases and billing mistakes</h2>
          <p>
            If you believe you were charged twice in error or billed incorrectly, contact
            <a href="mailto:contact@adschecks.com">contact@adschecks.com</a> promptly with the billing reference and any
            relevant account details.
          </p>
          <p>
            Duplicate or clearly accidental charges may be reviewed individually and, where confirmed, may be corrected or
            refunded.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Dispute review basis</h2>
          <p>For commercial or billing disputes, AdsChecks reviews the following evidence package references:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>run ID</li>
            <li>verification status</li>
            <li>artifacts such as screenshots and JSON metadata</li>
            <li>timestamp</li>
            <li>check context including GEO and device</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-card">
          <h2>Contact route</h2>
          <p>
            Send refund or billing questions to <a href="mailto:contact@adschecks.com">contact@adschecks.com</a>. Include
            enough detail for the charge and run to be identified and reviewed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
